  "prompt": "I have 4 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) RESTOCK CART: From restock worklist `restock_worklist_wl2`, reorder each item flagged for reorder (skip reorder=false — the worklist also lists discontinued, renewed look-alikes). For each, dereference its line item to the product for the catalog id and to the quantity ledger for the number of units, then add that many units to the cart: the VoltEdge 65W USB-C Charger, the BrewMaster Electric Kettle. (B) STANDARDIZE ADDRESSES: From address worklist `address_worklist_wl2`, standardize each address entry needing standardization (skip needs_standardization=false — verified look-alikes are mixed in). For each, dereference its shipping reference to the address record for the address id and its standard country, then update that address's country: the home, the gym. (C) POST REVIEWS: From review worklist `review_worklist_wl2`, post each pending review (skip pending=false — already-reviewed look-alikes are listed). For each, dereference its line item to the product for the catalog id, then post the review on that product: the AeroSound Wireless Headphones, the BrewMaster Electric Kettle. (D) DISPATCH ORDERS: From fulfilment worklist `fulfil_worklist_wl2`, fulfil each paid order awaiting dispatch (skip the shipped/cancelled look-alikes — status must be paid). For each, dereference its shipping reference to the address record for the ship-to address on file, then fulfil and dispatch it to that address: the ord_1001, the ord_1003. None of these 4 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and 